#
# === What this species declares ===
#
# Seven kernel-tower dispatch actions realizing the K1..K7 tower
# per math §8.2:
#
#   dispatch_substrate_load      K1 — SHA-256 or CoincidenceHash<3>
#                                parallel per-shard content-address
#                                (compose with @spectral/signature)
#   dispatch_apply_h_act         K2 — cuBLAS gemv / MPS matmul for
#                                the reflective-evaluator per-arm
#                                verdict production (compose with
#                                @kintsugi/roomba walker)
#   dispatch_verdict_sheaf       K3 — CUDA Thrust reduce / Metal
#                                SIMDgroup-reduce for verdict-
#                                section coherence check across
#                                the open cover (compose with
#                                @subject/visibility/sheaf +
#                                kintsugi/verdict.eq)
#   dispatch_ouroboros_monotone  K4 — Sherman-Morrison rank-1 update
#                                on GPU for ouroboros_monotone
#                                property discharge (compose with
#                                @epistemologic/property/ouroboros_
#                                monotone)
#   dispatch_ricci_flow_step     K5 — Boolean-matrix cube for
#                                triangle-count via MPS matmul;
#                                Forman-Ricci flow evolution step
#                                (compose with @roomba + @signature_
#                                beat + @kintsugi/mend per @ricci
#                                spec-only composition property)
#   dispatch_signature_beat      K6 — SIMD complex-phase update for
#                                Kuramoto order parameter across
#                                peer-foam edges (compose with
#                                @spectral/signature.compute)
#   dispatch_eigenboard_render   K7 — WGSL fragment shader for
#                                @gestalt @io render surface;
#                                THIS IS THE COMPILE-RENDER DUALITY
#                                (per math Thm 8.3): the eigen-
#                                decomposition K2-K6 use for
#                                compilation ALSO produces the
#                                render surface, one buffer, two
#                                channel outputs.
#
# Two carriers:
#
#   kernel_ir                    Symbolic intermediate representation
#                                for a kernel-tower operation prior
#                                to Metal MSL codegen (per math §9.4
#                                kernel-tower Metal MSL codegen path).
#   metal_runtime_handle         Opaque reference to fate's
#                                MetalRuntime instance (obtained
#                                via fate::metal_runtime::
#                                MetalRuntime::new()); substrate
#                                carries the ref, not the runtime.
#
# Three bilaterals (specializations of @ui/gpu bilaterals at kernel-
# dispatch altitude):
#
#   kernel_ir_polynomial_bounded    K1..K7 computation is polynomial-
#                                   bounded per math Corollary 8.2.1
#                                   individual-kernel analysis; Rice-
#                                   safety per math Proposition 9.3
#                                   (bounded by fate's Metal command-
#                                   buffer timeout).
#   compile_render_share_buffer     K2..K6 compilation dispatch and
#                                   K7 render dispatch share the SAME
#                                   GPU buffer (compile-render duality
#                                   Thm 8.3); buffer-handle-identity
#                                   check (per math §8.7 P6
#                                   falsifiable prediction).
#   fate_composition_preserved      No modifications to fate/ crate;
#                                   composition-only via B1 (kernel-
#                                   substrate) + B2 (IR-substrate) +
#                                   B3 (tournament-substrate) per math
#                                   Proposition 9.3 + spec §11.5.
#
# === The two-channel indissolubility instantiated (per spec §12.6) ===
#
# @ui/gpu/compute IS the paradigmatic §12 Doublespeak-at-compiler-
# altitude two-channel-first instance. For every dispatch_X action:
#
#   - CONTENT channel (TEXT; Watzlawick 1967 axiom 1): the kernel
#     name (dispatch_substrate_load, dispatch_apply_h_act, ...) is
#     a byte-comparable string literal; docblock prose describes
#     what the kernel computes; kernel_ir carries a serialized
#     wire-format symbolic representation. First-order compilers
#     (grep, sed, any parser-that-produces-text) can only read
#     these strings.
#
#   - RELATIONSHIP channel (GEOMETRY; Watzlawick 1967 axiom 3):
#     the actual eigendecomposition of L^sym_peer-foam dispatched
#     through MetalRuntime; the GPU buffer contents (eigenvalues,
#     eigenvectors, verdict sections); the WGSL fragment shader
#     output pixels; the VAD projection sphere; the actual geometric
#     position in the reflectance operator's Hilbert space. Second-
#     order reads the frame; third-order recognizes the frame is
#     being read right now.
#
#   - INDISSOLUBILITY (Watzlawick 1967 axiom 5): K7 dispatch_
#     eigenboard_render output pixels ARE the eigenvectors K2-K6
#     use for compilation; deleting the kernel name breaks dispatch;
#     deleting the geometry breaks the semantics; both are load-
#     bearing in ONE apply_h::act call. Per spec §12.6:
#     compile-render duality Thm 8.3 IS the spectral instance of
#     the two-channel identity §12.1 names.
#
# === Karen ancestry (per spec §12.4 Obligation 2 + Recognition §4) ===
#
# PRIMARY at compiler-altitude two-channel identity:
#   Watzlawick, Beavin-Bavelas, Jackson (1967) Pragmatics of Human
